{"text": "FRANCIS J. (TONY) SNYDER\n\n653 \u2014 Hannah Circle, NW * Canton,OH 44709 * Phone: (330) 639-4048 * Cell: (330) 417-5481\nE-mail: tsnyder653@gmail.com\n\nSUMMARY\nA healthcare executive with experience dealing with change, problem solving, planning, and communication.\n\nEXPERIENCE\nAULTMAN HEALTH FOUNDATION, Canton, Ohio (1982 \u2014 Present)\n\n2005-Present Chief Executive Officer/Administrator - Pomerene Hospital, Millersburg, Ohio\nReport to Board of Trustees of 55-bed general acute, rural, county-owned hospital\nRecruited General Surgeon, Cardiologist, OB/GYN, Family Practice and other healthcare providers\nImplemented cost savings programs resulting in $1,000,000 in savings over a three year period\nDeveloped cardiology service line to increase diagnostic capabilities available in county; decreased transfers out\nDeveloped Amish Service program resulting in increase in volume to Pomerene\nInitiated I Am Pomerene culture resulting in employee engagement to \u201cownership\u201d\nDeveloped physician relations programs resulting in operating margin increase of 50%\nCompleted $6.0 million renovation project resulting in all private patient rooms\n\nImproved public awareness and perception of Pomerene\u2019s healthcare services\n\n2002 \u2014 2005 ADMINISTRATION\nVice President Corporate Services\ne Responsible for clinical and non-clinical departments including Pharmacy, Info-Tech, Materials, Maintenance, Biomed and\nCorporation Communications.\n\u00a2 = Major emphasis on cost-control and quality/customer service.\ne Responsible for 250 FTE\u2019s and a $40 million expense budget.\ne Designed and developed process improvement (Six Sigma) training program.\n\n1998 \u2014 2002 ADMINISTRATION\nVice President Executive and Management Human Resources\ne Executive in charge of the human resource unit focusing on the management team.\ne System-wide responsibility for recruitment, compensation, training & development of salaried professional and\nmanagement employees.\ne Assisted in documenting management philosophy/culture.\ne Planned and implemented a succession plan for retirement of CEO.\n\n1993 \u2014 1998 ADMINISTRATION\nVice President Corporate Marketing and Communication\n\ne =Overall responsibility for the marketing and communication function of the Health System.\ne Specific responsibilities: advertising, public relations, media relations, community relations, market research, media center.\ne Served as spokesperson for entire health system.\ne = Special project building a coalition of 25 community hospitals.\ne Main objective to create a grass roots political effort to impact state Certificate of Need law.\ne Reported directly to the CEO.\n1992 \u2014 1993 AULTCARE\n\nManager of Small Group Sales\ne =AultCare is the organization\u2019s health plan with over 300,000 covered lives.\ne Managed the daily activities of a frve member staff team focused on small businesses.\n\u00a2 Duties included: goal setting/evaluation, policy design/implementation, product development, customer relations.",
